	abstract = {In this Letter we report the investigation of transport and static properties of a Bose-Einstein condensate in a large-spaced optical lattice. The lattice spacing can be easily tuned starting from few micrometers by adjusting the relative angle of two partially reflective mirrors. We have performed in-situ imaging of the atoms trapped in the potential wells of a 20 µm spaced lattice. For a lattice spacing of 10 µm we have studied the transport properties of the system and the interference pattern after expansion, evidencing quite different results with respect to the physics of {BECs} in ordinary near-infrared standing wave lattices, owing to the different length and energy scales.},
